# Grand tour for iomoon -- every mode, award and sequence the rules describe,
# in the order the machine allows them.
#
# TWO BALLS, because the drop bank resets only at ball start (rules 3.3.6): a
# drop-dependent award started with the bank already flat cannot be completed,
# and Special Drop Probe needs five STANDING targets to knock down, while
# Special Drop Target wants them standing too.  So ball 1 leaves the bank alone
# and ball 2 flattens it deliberately.
#
# BALL 1 -- ORBITS, then the Monolith cycle
#   Six lane-4 / bull's-eye-1 pairs put [413C:0102] at its cap of 6.  That gates
#   three things (rules 3.3.7/3.3.3): Jupiter retaining a ball at all, LPA3
#   (Little Multiball) being lightable on the Monolith, and lane 10's larger
#   award.  Without it LPA3 never lights and the cycle can only ever show nine
#   of its ten positions.
#   Then fourteen rounds of {lane 6 to arm, one bumper to step, scoop 1 to
#   cash, play}.  The burst is 20 bumper hits (Impact Count wants 20 inside its
#   15 s, and 20 is cycle-neutral so the walk stays aligned), both ramps and
#   scoop 2.  Ramp 1 during Orbit Flip is what lights LBH, Black Hole Power.
#   Deliberately NO drop targets in this burst: they would flatten the bank and
#   make Special Drop Target worthless for the rest of the ball.
#   Then a Jupiter lock and scoop 1, which is how LPA3 pays out -- Little
#   Multiball is awarded at Jupiter, not at the scoop (rules 3.3.3/3.2.6).
#
# BALL 2 -- the bank, and the two-lock modes
#   ORBITS again, then all five drop targets plus the inner target, which with
#   the bank already flat is what starts Special Drop Probe (rules 3.2.7).
#   Then two Jupiter locks with the bank DOWN, which is Wonderful Thing rather
#   than Multiball (rules 3.3.7) -- the one two-lock mode the multiball capture
#   does not cover, since that one leaves the bank standing.
#   Finally both shooters, which alternate LPA11 / LPA12 (Lagrange Scape /
#   Lagrange Orbit), the pair that is never cashed.
#
# Needs a seeded NVRAM with credits -- see dmd/multiball/README.md.
